# Build output (delivered via GitHub Release assets for HACS)
dist/

# Generated figures. The tracked set is exactly what README.md references and
# nothing else: each figure is displayed as a theme-adaptive SVG and links
# through to its light PNG.
#
# The link target must be the PNG. raw.githubusercontent.com serves SVG with
# `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'`, which permits style-src but
# blocks img-src — and these SVGs contain nothing but two base64 <image>
# elements, so navigating straight to one renders a blank page. Embedding via
# <img> is unaffected, which is why the README displays fine while a direct
# link would not.
#
# Everything else — dark PNGs, unreferenced figures, verification frames,
# motion captures — is a build artifact, deterministically regenerable with
# `npm run screenshot:hero`. See scripts/screenshot.js + encode-adaptive-svgs.sh.
img/*
!img/hero-adaptive.svg
!img/hero-light.webp
!img/themes-adaptive.svg
!img/themes-light.webp
!img/surface-theming-adaptive.svg
!img/surface-theming-light.webp

